<text layer="alpha1" matrix="1 0 0 1 -160.793 166.207" transformations="translations" pos="240 80" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="160" height="20.9244" depth="6.972" valign="top">$t = \sum P / 2$</text>
<text layer="phi" matrix="1 0 0 1 -32 164" transformations="translations" pos="48 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="832" height="36.0948" depth="22.176" valign="top">\textbf{Theorem 2.} \hl{Empty Hexasort} on spider graphs with nine vertices and four colors is weakly NP-hard.</text>
<text layer="psi" matrix="1 0 0 1 -96 108" transformations="translations" pos="240 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="688" height="20.9244" depth="6.972" valign="top">$ \langle \text{1 \cred stack},  \text{1 \cblue stack} \rangle $</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 -92 141" transformations="translations" pos="240 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="688" height="17.6904" depth="3.696" valign="top">$S +$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 -160 180" transformations="translations" pos="240 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="688" height="20.944" depth="7" valign="top">$S&apos; =  \langle \text{2 \cred stacks}, \text{2 \cblue stacks}, \text{4 \cgreen stacks}  \rangle + $</text>
<text layer="zeta" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -16" transformations="translations" pos="64 96" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="816" height="19.3928" depth="5.404" valign="top">The first two red stacks have to be placed exactly one vertex apart.</text>
