<text layer="epsilon" matrix="1 0 0 1 -32 48" transformations="translations" pos="48 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="832" height="36.0948" depth="22.176" valign="top">\textbf{Theorem 3.} \hl{Empty Hexasort} on the disjoint union of spider graphs with ten vertices each is strongly NP-hard.</text>
<text layer="delta" matrix="1 0 0 1 -32 48" transformations="translations" pos="48 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="832" height="36.0948" depth="22.176" valign="top">By the pigeon-hole principle, each gadget must be assigned the colorful stacks shown in the first configuration.</text>
<text layer="beta" matrix="1 0 0 1 544 99.9997" transformations="translations" pos="240 80" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="160" height="17.6904" depth="3.696" valign="top">$t = B + 4$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 -166.263 6.99971" transformations="translations" pos="240 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="624" height="20.9244" depth="6.972" valign="top">$\langle \text{2 \cred stacks}, \text{2 \cblue stacks}, \text{2 \cgreen stacks} \rangle \times m$ + </text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0.00045668 5.99971" transformations="translations" pos="73.7366 143.705" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="163.54" height="18.5976" depth="4.648" valign="top">$S_A +$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0.61068 7.99971" transformations="translations" pos="73.1264 111.364" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="747.034" height="20.9244" depth="6.972" valign="top">$\langle \text{1 \cred stack}, \text{1 \cblue stack}, \text{1 \cgreen stack}, \text{ 4 black stacks} \rangle \times m$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 -63.9995 5.99971" transformations="translations" pos="73.7366 143.705" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="163.54" height="16.5144" depth="2.548" valign="top">$S$ = </text>
