<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -40.3" pin="h" transformations="translations" pos="0 524" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="788" height="66.8192" depth="52.976" valign="top" style="itemize">\item  Is based on the previous reduction from 3-partition
\item The sequence and threshold stay the same; only the graph structure changes.
\item The connectors do not create new useful interactions.</text>
<text layer="gamma" matrix="1 0 0 1 -32 135.7" transformations="translations" pos="48 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="832" height="36.0948" depth="22.176" valign="top">\textbf{Theorem 4.} \hl{Empty Hexasort} on trees of bounded height or degree is strongly NP-hard.</text>
