<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -48" pin="h" transformations="translations" pos="0 524" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="920" height="86.2568" depth="72.436" valign="top">Takeaways:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Empty Hexasort is computationally hard
    \item Weakly NP-hardness already with tiny graphs and one color
    \item Strong NP-hardness persist on restricted graph classes
    \item Bounded settings admit polynomial-time algorithms
\end{itemize}</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" pin="h" transformations="translations" pos="0 269.307" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="920" height="70.294" depth="56.476" valign="top">Open directions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Multicolored stacks as in playable versions
    \item Empty Hexasort tractability for bounded $t$ and bounded $|C|$
    \item Strong NP-hardness for constant $|C|$
\end{itemize}</text>
</page>
